declare cid uuid;
begin
  select id into cid from public.courses where slug = 'bib-101';
  insert into public.course_items (course_id, kind, position, title, content) select cid, 'topic', 23, $j$6.3 Sacrifice, Priesthood and the Prophet like Moses$j$, $j${"readings": [{"title": "Genesis 22 (King James Version)", "url": "/portal/bible/Genesis/22"}, {"title": "Leviticus 16 (King James Version)", "url": "/portal/bible/Leviticus/16"}, {"title": "Leviticus 17 (King James Version)", "url": "/portal/bible/Leviticus/17"}, {"title": "Deuteronomy 18 (King James Version)", "url": "/portal/bible/Deuteronomy/18"}, {"title": "John 1 (King James Version)", "url": "/portal/bible/John/1"}], "body": "Read Genesis 22:1 to 14, Leviticus 16 and 17:11, Deuteronomy 18:15 to 19 and John 1 in the King James Version. Then read this lesson.\n\nThe sacrifices, priests and feasts of the Old Testament taught Israel that sin is serious and that forgiveness comes at a cost. On Mount Moriah Abraham told Isaac that God would provide Himself a lamb. At the Passover a lamb's blood marked each house. On the Day of Atonement the high priest brought blood into the holy place. Leviticus 17:11 says that the life of the flesh is in the blood and that blood makes an atonement for the soul. Moses also promised a Prophet like himself whom the people must hear. The New Testament shows that Jesus Christ is the Lamb of God, the High Priest and the Prophet that Moses promised.\n\nKey words: sacrifice, atonement, blood, priest, Lamb.\n\nYour task: (1) Tell what Abraham said God would provide in Genesis 22:8. (2) Explain why blood was used in the sacrifices (Leviticus 17:11). (3) Write what John the Baptist said when he saw Jesus (John 1:29).\n\nCourse area: Bible elective. Scripture is read from the King James Version.", "video": "", "presenter": "Dr. Alex L. Jenkins Sr.", "standards": "Bible elective", "script": "Today we look at the sacrifices, the priests and the prophet that the Law promised. These pictures can seem strange at first, but they were teaching Israel something very important. Sin is serious, and forgiveness has a cost.\n\nGo back to the story of Abraham and Isaac on Mount Moriah. God told Abraham to offer his son. As they walked up the mountain, Isaac asked, Behold the fire and the wood: but where is the lamb for a burnt offering? Abraham answered in Genesis 22:8, My son, God will provide himself a lamb for a burnt offering. At the last moment God stopped Abraham and provided a ram caught in a thicket. Abraham had spoken more than he knew.\n\nThink again about the Passover. In Exodus 12:13 God said, when I see the blood, I will pass over you. The lamb died so that the household could live. Every year after that, Israel remembered that night.\n\nLeviticus gives the reason that blood was so important. Leviticus 17:11 says, For the life of the flesh is in the blood: and I have given it to you upon the altar to make an atonement for your souls. Atonement means covering for sin. Once a year, on the Day of Atonement, the high priest took blood into the most holy place for the sins of the nation. But the sacrifices had to be repeated again and again, which showed that they pointed to something greater.\n\nMoses also gave a promise about a prophet. In Deuteronomy 18:15 he said, The LORD thy God will raise up unto thee a Prophet from the midst of thee, of thy brethren, like unto me; unto him ye shall hearken. Moses was a deliverer, a lawgiver and a mediator. The Prophet to come would be all of that and more.\n\nWhen John the Baptist saw Jesus coming to him, he said these words. John 1:29 says, Behold the Lamb of God, which taketh away the sin of the world. The lamb of the Passover, the lamb that Abraham promised, the offerings of the altar and the sacrifices of the Day of Atonement all pointed to Jesus Christ, who gave His life for the sins of the world. He is also our High Priest and the Prophet that Moses promised.\n\nYour task is to tell what Abraham said God would provide, explain why blood was used in the sacrifices, and write what John the Baptist said when he saw Jesus. Then take the four question check.\n\nThe sacrifices pointed to the Savior who would give His life for us. Excellence, Faith, Purpose. I will see you in the next lesson."}$j$::jsonb where not exists (select 1 from public.course_items where course_id = cid and kind = 'topic' and title = $j$6.3 Sacrifice, Priesthood and the Prophet like Moses$j$);
end
$seed$;
